 "transcript": "This QR code lost a corner, and it still scans. Every QR code carries extra recovery data, error correction. If squares get torn or dirty, the scanner rebuilds the missing data. Level L recovers about 7% of its data. Level H about 30. But error correction can't fix the three corner squares scanners look for. Printing one, choose a higher level and keep those corners clear. Follow TensorBlue for software explained simply.",
